## `entry_hash` — DC-3, and validated before it was written

`entry_hash` is **DC-3**, declared at `framework.manifest.json`
`metadata.reproducible.digest_constructions.ledger_entry_hash` by `AIEF-AMD-008` §AMD-17,
disposing `ecr/ECR-Q-002`. Seven covered fields in the declared order — `seq`, `timestamp`,
`session_id`, `actor`, `action`, `artifacts`, `prev_hash` — each as one
`<field-name> <SP> <value> <LF>` record, concatenated with no header or trailer.
`entry_hash` is excluded from its own preimage.

`prev_hash` carries `L-0000001`'s `entry_hash` and is itself a covered field, which is what
makes the chain tamper-evident rather than merely sequential: altering entry 1 invalidates
entry 2's digest as well as its own.

**The implementation was re-validated against three controls before this entry was written**:
both worked examples the manifest publishes (`entry_1` → `cb8e7972…8259e0`, `entry_2` →
`66e51617…f8195b`), and — the stronger control — **`L-0000001` recomputed from its own
on-disk bytes to `7b76b9e1…aba712d5`**, the value `HEAD` carries. A construction that
reproduces the repository's own prior entry is not a construction that was guessed at.

